{
  "compilerObjectNote": "Typecheck-only config for the Remote main-process modules AND the engine-overrides main-process modules. Not used by the engine build (which has its own tsconfig + real electron).",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "Bundler",
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    "strict": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": [
    "typecheck/electron-stub.d.ts",
    "electron/remote/**/*.ts",
    "electron/remote-preload.ts",
    // engine-overrides/electron/ had NO standing typecheck coverage at all,
    // which is how a whole feature's worth of main-process code (the meeting
    // notetaker: notetakerInit.ts, notetakerController.ts, notetakerSession.ts,
    // meetingWatcher.ts, meetingApps.ts, browserTabWatcher.ts) shipped with
    // `require()` calls, type casts and TS-narrowing subtleties that only a
    // human reading the diff would catch. It is covered now.
    "engine-overrides/electron/**/*.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "electron/remote/**/*.test.ts",
    "electron/remote/probe/**",
    "engine-overrides/electron/**/*.test.ts",

    // ─── OSS-ENGINE OVERLAY FILES — NOT TYPECHECKABLE FROM THIS REPO ───
    //
    // These are not standalone modules: they are patched REPLACEMENTS for
    // files in the cloned OSS engine, and they import siblings that only exist
    // in the wired tree (./api, ./audio, ./windowManager, ./ffmpeg, ./prompts,
    // ./keyStore, ./paywall/*, better-sqlite3, …). build/wire-into-engine.sh
    // copies them into work/oss-engine/electron/, and only THERE do their
    // imports resolve; here each one is an unavoidable TS2307 wall (38 errors
    // in sessionManager.ts alone) that would drown out every real finding on
    // the files above. Same pre-existing limitation that keeps
    // keyboard.notetaker.test.ts out of the default `npm test` glob — see the
    // header comment on that file.
    //
    // The last two are excluded only because they IMPORT overlay files
    // (dictation-recovery.ts → ./db + ./parakeet, whisper.ts → ./parakeet):
    // `exclude` does not stop a transitive pull-in, so they have to go too or
    // their imports come back as errors under someone else's name.
    "engine-overrides/electron/buildOSSAdapter.ts",
    "engine-overrides/electron/clipboard.ts",
    "engine-overrides/electron/db.ts",
    "engine-overrides/electron/parakeet.ts",
    "engine-overrides/electron/sessionManager.ts",
    "engine-overrides/electron/dictation-recovery.ts",
    "engine-overrides/electron/whisper.ts"

    // NOT EXCLUDABLE: keyboard.ts. It is an overlay file too (its
    // './paywall/remote/capture/agentGesture' import only resolves post-wire),
    // but notetakerInit.ts — the single highest-integration-risk file in the
    // notetaker feature, and the main reason this include exists — imports
    // `keyboardManager` from it, so it is pulled in transitively no matter
    // what. It contributes exactly two errors, BOTH pre-existing and both
    // deliberately left alone: the post-wire import path above, and a
    // duplicate `lastAgentToggleTime` field declaration introduced in f26beba,
    // long before the notetaker branch. `tsc`'s exit code here was ALREADY
    // non-zero before this include was added (two long-standing errors in
    // electron/remote/init.ts), so this config has never been a green gate —
    // it is a "read the list" tool, and the list is now much shorter than the
    // 48 errors a naive whole-directory include produces.
  ]
}
